<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37677" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-lambo</span></b> , ĕre, v.
			a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				lick</i> or <i>taste beforehand</i> or <i>first</i> (<b>poet.</b>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(mus) praelambens omne, quod affert,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 6, 109</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to wash</i> or <i>touch lightly</i>, <i>to bathe
			gently</i>, of a river that flows by a place: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arenas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Hamart. 357</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Avien. Perieg. 494</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
